WEBVTT

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:04.240
In the light

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.910
After all that, there was nothing?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.810
So Kaoru's our only hope?

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.250
Welcome back.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.280
Cold outside?

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.210
Welcome home!

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.340
How was it?

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.990
There are just days like this.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.390
So it was no use?

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:14.630
And you?

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.390
Nothing for us either.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.430
The ice on the river was too thick, so we couldn't catch any fish.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:20.590
I see.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.060
A zero harvest day.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.240
How many days in a row does this make?

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.200
Who has cooking duty today?

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:33.150
It's me.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.300
What's wrong?

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.780
I sprained my ankle earlier.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.840
But it's nothing serious.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.400
No, I'll take care of cooking today.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.760
What's on the menu?

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.350
Let's see...

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.130
I'll make soup with potatoes and dried meat.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.890
That again?

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:57.300
It sounds fine, but I almost can't eat that anymore.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.760
I could even go for a steak made of Pague.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.880
And even Adam would eat until he was stuffed.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.450
No, I wouldn't eat it!

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.450
Howard, don't be ridiculous!

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.990
Yes, it's mean to Adam.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.390
It was a joke!

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.130
But the way food is running out...

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.280
...we'll have to think about the worst-case scenario.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.210
Now, now...

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.790
Let's all cheer up!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.100
Right, right!

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.840
"There's always a blue sky in your heart."

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.790
The words of a great person.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.360
Whose words were they?

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.830
Mine!

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.030
Idiotic.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:38.850
What'dya say?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.390
Where are you going?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:45.900
I'll give it another try.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:47.290
Right now?

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.880
Great! That's our Kaoru!

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.150
We'll be waiting for you!

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:51.980
Howard!

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.490
It'll be pitch dark soon.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.590
I'll be back before then.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.310
Promise us.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:01.580
Be careful.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:55.800
Damn it...

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.450
Let's hurry up and eat.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.290
Once Kaoru gets back.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.810
For crying out loud, what's he up to?

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.850
He's searchin' for food, ain't he?

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:13.160
You even sent him off by saying, "We'll be waiting for you," Howard.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:17.440
That may be true, but I didn't tell him he could be late for dinner.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.310
Maybe something happened to him.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:21.310
I'll go look for him.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.490
I'll go too.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:26.850
That's impossible!

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.850
You sprained your ankle, didn't you?

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:30.450
I'm fine!

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.290
I'll go too!

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.730
I'll go by myself.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.940
Everyone else, start eating ahead of us.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.360
Just in case, you should take some live embers and oil.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.260
Luna, take this.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.940
Snowy nights...

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.740
...are bright, I guess.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.160
He climbed down here.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.190
It's started coming down strongly again.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.330
Will they be okay?

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:19.500
Luna...

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.930
It looks like my turn has finally come, Louis.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.450
Kaoru!

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:00.680
Kaoru!

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.230
Grab on to this quickly!

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:26.780
We made it!

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:27.710
Why are you here?

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:29.400
Why?

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:32.290
Isn't it obvious? I came looking for you.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.280
But you could have been in danger!

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.700
Now see here...

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.230
Let's go back.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.050
But to think there'd be that big a fissure in a place like that...

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:21.830
Kaoru!

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:26.550
Are you listening? It's dangerous to climb a cliff in this wind!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.410
Let's look for somewhere we can bivouac.

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:36.830
I'm going out after all!

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.660
In this blizzard?

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:39.900
Give it up!

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.900
Bell, I'll go with you!

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:42.860
No way.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.840
If someone goes out to search now...

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.130
...there's a danger they might be in an accident as well.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:53.060
I know you're worried about Luna and Kaoru...

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.340
...but I won't let you put yourself in danger right before our eyes.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:58.880
Menori...

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.660
We'll wait for them to come back.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.730
You even brought embers.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.510
Bell said I should bring them.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.250
And also, here.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:21.830
From Sharla.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.050
Sharla...

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.040
...got quite a shock.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:38.810
She told you?

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.030
I asked her.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:45.150
Because she'd been acting strangely.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:50.780
I believed there was no way you'd do something like that.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:56.700
And even if you had, there was surely some deeper reason behind it.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.460
There isn't one.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.990
I killed him.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.560
He was...

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.900
...the first opponent I ever lost to.

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:45.380
Before I came to Roca A-2 I lived in a space station.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:50.400
There was a training school for space pilots there.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:58.240
You are the superior students chosen from over ten thousand boys and girls.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.840
But your true battle begins now.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:07.840
Because in the five years until you graduate, you will be run through a sieve repeatedly...

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:13.310
...and in the end, only very few of you will be able to become space pilots.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.890
For the next problem, you are not to use the computer.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.290
Raise your hand when you're done.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:34.430
Done!

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.330
In the first year...

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:48.680
...the hundred and sixty students who entered were thinned by half...

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.560
...and halved again each year...

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.990
...so by the last school year we had been reduced to ten.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:15.750
To think my roommate in the last year of school would be Kaoru!

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.110
I'm delighted! Nice to meet you.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.930
I've actually wanted to be your friend for a while.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:21.830
Forget it!

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:25.500
I hated him.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.730
I couldn't get over how he could help the weaker students while handling everything perfectly.

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:36.710
I hated that smile of his too, overflowing with moral sense and never twisted by hardship.

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.960
Number eight, exhale more slowly.

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:04.500
If you want to give up, then go home.

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.940
There's plenty of other candidate trainees.

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:12.560
Hang on.

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:13.840
Let go of me!

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:15.450
I'm going home.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:18.000
I won't be in the last selection anyways.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:20.360
You can't give up on yourself!

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:23.210
If you do, you'll regret it your whole life!

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:29.740
We may be rivals, but we're also friends sharing the same dream.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:33.040
So stand up. We'll go talk to the teacher together.

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:41.180
Until the end, I thought the encouragement he would sometimes show was just an act for marks.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:45.940
So I planned to take that mask off him someday.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:33.560
Top scorer is Louis. Second place is Kaoru.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.450
But...

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:39.380
...he was perfect.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:49.910
From what I hear, they're only choosing one person in the last round.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:52.460
Just one person?

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:56.660
Which means it's a fight between Louis and Kaoru.

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:58.880
No, it's obviously Louis.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:03.190
Kaoru's lacking in leadership and cooperation ability.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:05.740
Hey!

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:20.930
Your final mission before the final selection will be piloting these training ships in groups of two.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.440
Please treat it as such.

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.540
First will be Louis and Kaoru.

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:26.590
Aye!

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:41.400
All ships!

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.100
Dust storm approaching!

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:45.750
This is not a drill!

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:47.360
Return immediately!

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:48.490
Roger!

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.480
Range: 30.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.910
We can't get out before the storm gets here.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:54.940
We'll just have to steer through it.

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:56.440
I'll pilot us.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.160
Right now, I'm the pilot!

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.390
But my piloting skills are better!

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.000
I won't lose at the real thing!

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:05.700
Fine.

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:08.740
Here they come.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.140
Next, angle 35.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.980
Approaching fast.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.660
Range: 10...

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:26.290
You're great!

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:33.230
This is bad!

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:48.040
Kaoru, let go!

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:51.110
If you don't, you'll die too!

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:05.630
Kaoru...

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:11.480
I leave my dream in your care.

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.100
Louis!

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:36.680
At the academy, there was a rumour that I let go intentionally to get my rival out of the way.

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:42.530
I didn't want to make up an excuse or anything.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.280
I decided to drop out of the academy.

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:58.240
Right now, he's still floating around the darkness of space.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:01.090
And he will forever.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:05.630
There's no reason I who killed him should be here in the light.

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:08.810
You didn't kill him, Kaoru.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.840
We might have both made it if Louis had been piloting.

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.890
My pointless pride killed him.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:19.500
But...

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.930
But, you didn't let go of that Louis kid's hand on purpose, right?

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:26.850
I'd never be so cowardly as to use an excuse like that!

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:32.360
But once in a while, a strange thought creeps over me.

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:38.780
Back then, why couldn't I hold on tighter?

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:41.550
Maybe...

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.040
...I let go unconsciously!

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:48.080
Kaoru...

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:12.230
The rope blew away somewhere.

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.960
Then we'll have to climb up by ourselves.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:55.500
Kaoru...

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:58.200
Don't let go!

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:14.210
Wait here.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:37.280
Can I ask you just one thing?

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:39.940
What is it?

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:42.190
What did Louis say at the end?

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:44.740
I don't know.

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:47.250
Even though I've been thinking about it all this time.

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:51.150
Maybe he said, "Live!"

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:56.030
My father said that at the end.

00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:59.510
He died to save my life.

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:00.830
So...

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:14.810
Live!

00:22:26.630 --> 00:22:27.260
Louis...

00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:36.600
--Luna!
--Kaoru!

00:22:37.130 --> 00:22:38.360
Luna!

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:42.190
Our friends are here.

00:22:42.490 --> 00:22:43.160
Let's go.

00:22:43.580 --> 00:22:44.250
Yeah.

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:06.380
Maybe these ruins are my home.

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:13.500
Chako and Shingo said the card that seems like it might open the ruins can only be used by me.

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:20.590
And why do the people who appear in my dream look at me so gently?

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:23.890
"Alduram Gyet?"

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:28.580
Next time: Who? Who is it?
